    summary: "Susan Clark heads the Cancer Epigenetics Laboratory at the Garvan Institute of Medical Research in Sydney. She developed the bisulphite sequencing method that made genome-wide DNA methylation mapping possible, and her group investigates epigenome remodelling in prostate and breast cancer and its use in biomarkers. She is a Fellow of the Australian Academy of Science.",
